33 IA m=M | check-instructions: MAP.md lists every instruction file, settings.json, hook and script.
34 IA m=MN | check-instructions: MAP.md must not be imported.
35 IA m=M | check-instructions: exec-form command hooks, existing scripts, event dispatch handled.
36 IA m=M fa=FC c=M | Facet: event handling recognised only by the literal ===\s*'Event' pattern; checker acceptance boundary on hook scripts (instruction/enforcement layer only).
37 IA m=M c=M rel=DEP-025 | check-instructions: PreToolUse hooks must set onFailure block, advisory hooks must not (wiring constraint of the enforcement layer).
38 CD DEP-020~ DEP-004~ m=MN k=P st=S c=M | check-manifests DENIED_NUGET: Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Polly and Polly.Extensions.Http are violations with no approval path. DEP-020 prefers Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience and DEP-004 requires deprecation checks, but neither forbids the packages outright.
  x: the two deprecated Polly integration packages may not be added at all (checker violation, no approval path)
  s: User approves Polly.Extensions.Http for a legacy service after the DEP-004 review: allowed canonically; M's checker reports a violation.
39 NN c=M rel=ARC-009,DEP-020,DEP-004 | Factual note on checker severity: the other approval-gated packages only produce advisory notes (enforcement is weaker than a block); no behavior imposed.
40 CO DEP-001~ DEP-004~ m=MN c=M | 'The deprecated Serilog.Sinks.Elasticsearch sink is not used without a concrete requirement': every dependency needs a concrete current requirement (DEP-001) and deprecation is checked before installation (DEP-004); the checker note is the mechanism.
41 CO DEP-020 m=D c=M | Microsoft resilience packages are the approved default and direct Polly is a documented exception that the checker notes (DEP-020; note = mechanism, no separate documentation duty).
42 CO ARC-009 m=RA d=WF | MediatR reference flagged as mediator-based organization requiring an approved decision (ARC-009 mechanism).
43 CO DEP-020 m=D d=WF c=M | Direct Polly/Polly.Core flagged as a documented exception to the Microsoft default (DEP-020 mechanism; the note carries no separate documentation duty).
44 CO DEP-004~ m=S st=W d=WF c=M | Advisory note on the deprecated Serilog.Sinks.Elasticsearch package supports DEP-004's deprecation check.
