47 CD ARC-001 m=M k=W st=S c=M | Checker enforces the ARC-001 production graph; it additionally reports any production->test project reference as a violation, which ARC-001's layer rules do not address.
  x: production projects referencing test projects are checker violations
  s: An Api project referencing a shared TestSupport project for a development-only endpoint: not covered by ARC-001's layer list; M's checker reports a violation.
48 CO ARC-028~ m=M d=WF c=M | Checker limits test references to the tested layer and layers inward of it (ARC-028 mechanism; weaker than the rule's allow-list, which it does not fully enforce).
49 CO DEP-006 m=M d=WF c=M | CPM violations (no ManagePackageVersionsCentrally, opt-out, references without Directory.Packages.props, PackageVersion without Version, versions in project files) enforce DEP-006; VersionOverride stays the sanctioned exception path.
50 CD DEP-003 m=MN k=W st=S c=M | Replica wording: pin the latest stable compatible version; missing/floating/range versions are violations; prerelease only when explicitly requested. DEP-003's explicit-request exception is honoured only for prerelease, not for floating versions.
  x: floating/range versions are violations even when explicitly requested
  s: User explicitly asks for a floating NuGet version: DEP-003 allows it; M's checker reports a violation.
51 CD DEP-003 m=MN k=W st=S | Same decision as calibration: always violations, no explicit-request exception, incl. exact bracket pins.
  x: Floating/range versions are always checker violations, with no explicit-request exception (NuGet '*', '[', '(' or ',' incl. exact bracket pins; npm empty/*/x/latest/next/>=)
  s: User explicitly asks for "8.*" of a package: DEP-003 allows it; the M checker still reports a violation the agent is told to address.
  fhd: Whether the explicit-request exception of DEP-003 should also be honoured by the manifest checker (checker vs skill text tension, Step-1 APPARENT_CONFLICT with FG-M-9c1350e27f).
52 CD DEP-003 m=MN k=W st=S | Prerelease noted as allowed only when explicitly requested (matches DEP-003); floating/range versions are violations without that exception.
